      "widgets_values": [
        "【FilmDateStamp Official Workflow】\n\nA specialized node designed to authentically simulate the physical exposure of camera quartz date stamps burned into photographic film emulsion.\n\n■ Quick Start:\n1. Select a style preset from `style_preset` (Japanese Tokyo 90s, American West Coast, European Classic, etc.) to automatically configure typography, emission spectrum, exposure, and formatting.\n2. Manually adjusting any parameter automatically switches to \"Custom\" for fine-tuning.\n\n■ Date Input (`date_string`):\n- Enter any text directly to stamp custom strings (e.g. `'98 12 24`).\n- Enter `auto` or `today` to generate the current runtime date.\n- Enter `random` to generate a random vintage date (1985–2005) with reproducible seed control.\n- Set `show_time` to True to append timestamps (HH:MM).\n\n■ Key Features:\n1. Authentic Hardware Fonts (FDS7Strict / FDSDotStrict / FDSMechanical70s):\n   - 1970s mechanical engraving (DIN 1451/JIS), 1980s 7-segment LED, and 1990s 5×7 capsule dots faithfully reproduced from vintage cameras.\n2. Optical Burn-in Model:\n   - Linear-space emulsion headroom synthesis. Over bright or white highlights, the stamp naturally blows out and blends seamlessly into saturated emulsion.\n3. Multi-Scale PSF & Halation:\n   - Saturated white core + spectral emission + red backplate halation with 3-tier organic irregularities (macro, meso, micro)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
